21	- [ ] **Step 3: Verify generated files open with the doctype**
22	
23	Run:
24	```bash
25	head -1 pan-african-org/fr/index.html pan-african-org/es/index.html
26	```
27	Expected: `<!DOCTYPE html>` on both. If a banner comes first, the charset bug is back — accented characters will corrupt in the video build.
28	
29	- [ ] **Step 4: Write the layout spec**
30	
31	Create `tests/org-layout.spec.js`:
32	
33	```js
34	const { test, expect } = require('@playwright/test');
35	const path = require('node:path');
36	const fs = require('node:fs');
37	
38	const ROOT = path.join(__dirname, '..', 'pan-african-org');
39	const PAGES = fs.readdirSync(path.join(ROOT, 'en')).filter((f) => f.endsWith('.html'));
40	
41	for (const locale of ['en', 'fr', 'es']) {
42	  for (const page of PAGES) {
43	    test(`[${locale}] ${page} renders without overflow or console errors`, async ({ page: p }) => {
44	      const errors = [];
45	      p.on('console', (m) => { if (m.type() === 'error') errors.push(m.text()); });
46	
47	      await p.setViewportSize({ width: 1920, height: 1080 });
48	      await p.goto('file://' + path.join(ROOT, locale, page));
49	      await p.waitForTimeout(300);
50	
51	      const overflow = await p.evaluate(() =>
52	        [...document.querySelectorAll('.sidebar, .topbar, .page-header, .nav-item')]
53	          .filter((el) => el.scrollWidth > el.clientWidth + 1)
54	          .map((el) => `${el.className}: ${el.scrollWidth}>${el.clientWidth}`)
55	      );
56	
57	      expect(errors, `console errors: ${errors.join(' | ')}`).toEqual([]);
58	      expect(overflow, `overflowing: ${overflow.join(' | ')}`).toEqual([]);
59	    });
60	  }
61	}
62	
63	test('language toggle preserves the current page across locales', async ({ page }) => {
64	  await page.goto('file://' + path.join(ROOT, 'fr', 'skill-gap.html'));
65	  const esHref = await page.getAttribute('a[hreflang="es"]', 'href');
66	  expect(esHref).toBe('../es/skill-gap.html');
67	  const enHref = await page.getAttribute('a[hreflang="en"]', 'href');
68	  expect(enHref).toBe('../en/skill-gap.html');
69	});
70	
71	test('every internal link resolves on disk', async () => {
72	  const missing = [];
73	  for (const locale of ['en', 'fr', 'es']) {
74	    for (const page of PAGES) {
75	      const html = fs.readFileSync(path.join(ROOT, locale, page), 'utf8');
76	      for (const m of html.matchAll(/href="([^"]+\.html)"/g)) {
77	        const target = path.resolve(path.join(ROOT, locale), m[1]);
78	        if (!fs.existsSync(target)) missing.push(`${locale}/${page} -> ${m[1]}`);
79	      }
80	    }
81	  }
82	  expect(missing, `broken links: ${missing.join(', ')}`).toEqual([]);
83	});
84	```
85	
86	- [ ] **Step 5: Run the layout spec**
87	
88	Run: `npx playwright test tests/org-layout.spec.js --reporter=list`
89	Expected: PASS. French runs 15–25% longer than English — if a nav item or button overflows, shorten the copy in the catalog rather than changing layout geometry.
90	
91	- [ ] **Step 6: Confirm the ministry site is still untouched**
92	
93	Run: `git status --porcelain fr/ es/ index.html tutorial-video/`
94	Expected: **empty output.**
95	
96	- [ ] **Step 7: Commit**
97	
98	```bash
99	git add pan-african-org tests/org-layout.spec.js
100	git commit -m "feat(org): generate French and Spanish site trees"
101	```
